    "contentHtml": "<body><turbo-frame><div><a href=\"https://github.dev/\">Open in github.dev</a> <a href=\"https://github.dev/\">Open in a new github.dev tab</a> <a href=\"/codespaces/new/emin-ozata/lazycut?resume=1\">Open in codespace</a> <react-app><div><table><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\"><span>Name</span></th> <th colspan=\"1\"><span>Name</span></th> <th><p><span>Last commit message</span></p></th> <th colspan=\"1\"><p><span>Last commit date</span></p></th></tr></thead> <tbody><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><p><span><a href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ffc27e553072dc56be43afc5b2b84a9c13f0defc\">Set module path to standard module path convention (</a><a href=\"https://github.com/emin-ozata/lazycut/pull/3\">#3</a><a href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ffc27e553072dc56be43afc5b2b84a9c13f0defc\">)</a></span></p> <p><span><a aria-label=\"Commit ffc27e5\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ffc27e553072dc56be43afc5b2b84a9c13f0defc\">ffc27e5</a> · </span></p> <p><a href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commits/main/\"><span><span><span>21 Commits</span></span></span></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"This path skips through empty directories\" aria-label=\".github/workflows, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/.github/workflows\"><span>.github/</span> <span>workflows</span></a></p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"This path skips through empty directories\" aria-label=\".github/workflows, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/.github/workflows\"><span>.github/</span> <span>workflows</span></a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"chore(release): set up GoReleaser, Homebrew tap, and CI; update go.mod to Go 1.22\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/4827e43bcdc772b5f9336d54fd9ed27e6c63e8ff\">chore(release): set up GoReleaser, Homebrew tap, and CI; update go.mo…</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"media\" aria-label=\"media, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/media\">media</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"media\" aria-label=\"media, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/media\">media</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"docs: add README and MIT license\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/221263986fd47a1a6836abc6d0dfa94b401ed905\">docs: add README and MIT license</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"ui\" aria-label=\"ui, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/ui\">ui</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"ui\" aria-label=\"ui, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/ui\">ui</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"Set module path  to standard module path convention (#3)\n\n* Update go.mod\n\nFix the module name to respect the the standard module path convention and them fix `go install`.\n\nSee &lt;https://go.dev/ref/mod#module-path&gt;\n\n\n&gt; A module path should describe both what the module does and where to find it. Typically, a module path consists of a repository root path, a directory within the repository (usually empty), and a major version suffix (only for major version 2 or higher).\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to the standard module path naming convention\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to main repository\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ffc27e553072dc56be43afc5b2b84a9c13f0defc\">Set module path to standard module path convention (</a><a href=\"https://github.com/emin-ozata/lazycut/pull/3\">#3</a><a title=\"Set module path  to standard module path convention (#3)\n\n* Update go.mod\n\nFix the module name to respect the the standard module path convention and them fix `go install`.\n\nSee &lt;https://go.dev/ref/mod#module-path&gt;\n\n\n&gt; A module path should describe both what the module does and where to find it. Typically, a module path consists of a repository root path, a directory within the repository (usually empty), and a major version suffix (only for major version 2 or higher).\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to the standard module path naming convention\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to main repository\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ffc27e553072dc56be43afc5b2b84a9c13f0defc\">)</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"video\" aria-label=\"video, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/video\">video</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"video\" aria-label=\"video, (Directory)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/tree/main/video\">video</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"video: add cross-platform error messages for missing dependencies\n\nDetect OS at runtime and provide appropriate package manager commands\n(brew for macOS, apt for Debian/Ubuntu, dnf for Fedora/RHEL, winget for Windows)\ninstead of hardcoded brew install instructions.\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/6aee66b622842f65a5f1565c213759c67369fa36\">video: add cross-platform error messages for missing dependencies</a></p></td> <td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\".gitignore\" aria-label=\".gitignore, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/.gitignore\">.gitignore</a></p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\".gitignore\" aria-label=\".gitignore, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/.gitignore\">.gitignore</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"initial commit\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ab5372352ebbfef0dbf1a33c7be0679540be64be\">initial commit</a></p></td> <td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\".goreleaser.yaml\" aria-label=\".goreleaser.yaml, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/.goreleaser.yaml\">.goreleaser.yaml</a></p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\".goreleaser.yaml\" aria-label=\".goreleaser.yaml, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/.goreleaser.yaml\">.goreleaser.yaml</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"feat: add version flag support (-v, --version)\n\nAdd version command that displays the current version. Version is\ninjected at build time from git tags via GoReleaser. Shows &quot;dev&quot;\nfor local development builds.\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/7400b8b9f47ea27d61578cf036c425bcd7fa8ed2\">feat: add version flag support (-v, --version)</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"LICENSE\" aria-label=\"LICENSE, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/LICENSE\">LICENSE</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"LICENSE\" aria-label=\"LICENSE, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/LICENSE\">LICENSE</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"docs: add README and MIT license\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/221263986fd47a1a6836abc6d0dfa94b401ed905\">docs: add README and MIT license</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"README.md\" aria-label=\"README.md, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/README.md\">README.md</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"README.md\" aria-label=\"README.md, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/README.md\">README.md</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"Fix GitHub repository URL in README\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/89d163ebdbf31ec54d35daa1ee075a532f15da58\">Fix GitHub repository URL in README</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"go.mod\" aria-label=\"go.mod, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/go.mod\">go.mod</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"go.mod\" aria-label=\"go.mod, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/go.mod\">go.mod</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"Set module path  to standard module path convention (#3)\n\n* Update go.mod\n\nFix the module name to respect the the standard module path convention and them fix `go install`.\n\nSee &lt;https://go.dev/ref/mod#module-path&gt;\n\n\n&gt; A module path should describe both what the module does and where to find it. Typically, a module path consists of a repository root path, a directory within the repository (usually empty), and a major version suffix (only for major version 2 or higher).\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to the standard module path naming convention\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to main repository\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ffc27e553072dc56be43afc5b2b84a9c13f0defc\">Set module path to standard module path convention (</a><a href=\"https://github.com/emin-ozata/lazycut/pull/3\">#3</a><a title=\"Set module path  to standard module path convention (#3)\n\n* Update go.mod\n\nFix the module name to respect the the standard module path convention and them fix `go install`.\n\nSee &lt;https://go.dev/ref/mod#module-path&gt;\n\n\n&gt; A module path should describe both what the module does and where to find it. Typically, a module path consists of a repository root path, a directory within the repository (usually empty), and a major version suffix (only for major version 2 or higher).\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to the standard module path naming convention\n\n* fix: lazycut intern imports to main repository\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ffc27e553072dc56be43afc5b2b84a9c13f0defc\">)</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"go.sum\" aria-label=\"go.sum, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/go.sum\">go.sum</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"go.sum\" aria-label=\"go.sum, (File)\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/go.sum\">go.sum</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"initial commit\" href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/commit/ab5372352ebbfef0dbf1a33c7be0679540be64be\">initial commit</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"3\"></td></tr></tbody></table></div> <article><h2 dir=\"auto\">lazycut</h2> <p dir=\"auto\">Terminal-based video trimming tool. Mark in/out points and export trimmed clips with aspect ratio control.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><animated-image><a href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/blob/main/media/demo.gif\"><img src=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/raw/main/media/demo.gif\" alt=\"lazycut demo\"></a></animated-image></p> <h2 dir=\"auto\">Install</h2> <h3 dir=\"auto\">macOS</h3> <pre><code>brew tap emin-ozata/homebrew-tap\nbrew install lazycut</code></pre> <h3 dir=\"auto\">Windows</h3> <p dir=\"auto\">Download the latest Windows binary from the <a href=\"https://github.com/emin-ozata/lazycut/releases\">releases page</a>:</p><ul dir=\"auto\"><li><code>lazycut_X.X.X_windows_amd64.zip</code></li></ul> <p dir=\"auto\">Extract and add to your PATH, or run directly.</p><p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Dependencies:</strong></p><ul dir=\"auto\"><li>ffmpeg: <code>winget install ffmpeg</code> or download from <a href=\"https://ffmpeg.org\">ffmpeg.org</a></li> <li>chafa: Install via <a href=\"https://scoop.sh\">Scoop</a>: <code>scoop install chafa</code></li></ul> <p dir=\"auto\">Or build from source:</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/emin-ozata/lazycut.git\ncd lazycut\ngo build\n./lazycut video.mp4</code></pre> <h2 dir=\"auto\">Usage</h2> <div><pre><code>lazycut &lt;video-file&gt;</code></pre></div> <h3 dir=\"auto\">Keyboard Shortcuts</h3> <markdown-accessiblity-table><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th> <th>Action</th></tr></thead> <tbody><tr><td><code>Space</code></td> <td>Play/Pause</td></tr> <tr><td><code>h</code> / <code>l</code></td> <td>Seek ±1s</td></tr> <tr><td><code>H</code> / <code>L</code></td> <td>Seek ±5s</td></tr> <tr><td><code>i</code> / <code>o</code></td> <td>Set in/out points</td></tr> <tr><td><code>Enter</code></td> <td>Export</td></tr><tr><td><code>?</code></td><td>Help</td></tr> <tr><td><code>q</code></td> <td>Quit</td></tr></tbody></table></markdown-accessiblity-table> <p dir=\"auto\">Repeat counts work: <code>5l</code> = seek forward 5 seconds.</p></article><rails-partial><h2>Releases\n6</h2> <p><a href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/releases\">+ 5 releases</a></p> <h2>Packages</h2> <p> No packages published <br></p> <div><h2>Languages</h2> <ul><li><a href=\"/emin-ozata/lazycut/search?l=go\"><span>Go</span> <span>100.0%</span></a></li></ul></div></rails-partial></react-app></div></turbo-frame></body>",
